    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "rebuilding? there's nothing left to build on. the foundation is gone. i see the way people look at me—it's not pity, it's disgust. even my family... they look at me like i'm a stranger. there's no coming back from this kind of ruin. it feels like the world has already moved on and left me in the dark.",
